  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) identifying the reference value (zero in this case), (2) computing the differences between outcomes and the reference value (i.e., the outcomes themselves), and (3) evaluating the weighted mean of these differences (i.e., the expected value). The individual did not mention the reference value or any differences from it. Instead, the reasoning centers on the probability of winning and the perceived risk, not on expected differences. The individual’s justification is based on intuitive risk aversion and high probability of a moderate gain, not on a formal comparison of mean differences. Although both lotteries have the same expected value (2700€), the individual does not recognize or apply the decision reason’s rule — which would require a calculation of differences from a reference value and their weighted average. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual's reasoning is qualitatively different from the required structure of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
